Continuing my DSA journey I solved two important Binary Tree problems that helped me strengthen my understanding of BFS, recursion and level wise traversal.
Day 45- Minimum Depth of Binary Tree(LeetCode 111)
 Approach:
I used Breadth-First Search (BFS) with a Queue.
The tree is processed level by level, and as soon as I encounter the first leaf node (a node with no left and right child), I return the current depth.
Using BFS is efficient here because the first leaf encountered is guaranteed to be at the minimum depth.
 Time Complexity: O(n)
 Space Complexity: O(n)-Queue can contain nodes from a level.
